==Swedish==
{{wikipedia|lang=sv}}
[[File:Musca_domestica_September_2007-1.jpg|thumb|250px|en fluga ({{l|sv|husfluga||housefly}}) ({{senseno|sv|insect}})]]
[[File:Fly lures.jpg|thumb|250px|flugor ({{senseno|sv|lure}})]]
[[File:Bowtie paisley red.jpg|thumb|250px|en fluga ({{senseno|sv|bowtie}})]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|flugha}}, from {{inh|sv|non|fluga||fly}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*flugǭ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|sv|Sv-en fluga.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|c}}

# {{senseid|sv|insect}} a [[fly]] (insect)
#: {{ux|sv|Flyg, fula '''fluga''', flyg! Och den fula '''flugan''' flög. [a tongue twister]|Fly [imperative of {{m|sv|flyga}}], ugly '''fly''', fly! And '''the''' ugly '''fly''' flew.}}
# {{senseid|sv|lure}} {{lb|sv|fishing}} a [[fly]] ([[lure]] resembling an insect)
# {{senseid|sv|bowtie}} a [[bowtie]]
# {{senseid|sv|fad}} a [[fad]], a [[craze]] (phenomenon that becomes popular for a short time)

====Usage notes====
Not necessarily as negative sounding as ''fad'' in ({{senseno|sv|fad}}) (though it sounds the same in "Det är bara en fluga" (It's just a fad) and the like). ''Craze'' is often closer in tone, leaning more tongue-in-cheek or the like.

